WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.610
Every handshake has two hands in it.

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.130
That small fact is surprisingly powerful.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.630
If each person reports how many hands they shook,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.680
and you add up the reports, every handshake has been

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.970
counted twice, once by each person.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.280
Counting something in two different ways gives you an

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.410
equation for free.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.060
It lets you count lines by counting ends, or faces by

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.550
counting edges, without drawing the whole picture.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.140
Six people meet, and everyone shakes hands once

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.130
with everyone else.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.210
How many handshakes take place?

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.250
Pause and think about what each person would report.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.710
Each person shakes hands with the five others,

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.890
so each person reports five.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.650
Six reports of five add to thirty.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.930
But each handshake was reported by both of the

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:49.640
people in it.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.180
So thirty counts every handshake twice.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.560
Thirty divided by two is fifteen handshakes.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.750
The same idea can prove something is impossible.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:01.320
Can seven people each shake hands with

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.490
exactly three others?

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.690
The reports would add to twenty-one.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.420
But the total of the reports is always twice the number

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.550
of handshakes, so it must be even.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:12.030
Twenty-one is odd.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.090
It cannot be done.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.570
It works for solids too.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.020
A cube has six faces, and each face has four

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.750
edges: twenty-four reports.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.470
Every edge belongs to two faces,

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.170
so there are twelve edges.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.410
Let each object report what it touches.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:29.670
Add the reports.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.210
Then divide by how many times each item was reported.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.840
Notebook challenge: in a tournament, eight teams each

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.430
play every other team once.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.090
How many games are played?
